      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Traditional investigative methods to detect and localise cardiac abnormalities are often difficult and time consuming. The use of minicomputers has made a dramatic impact on non-invasive diagnostic techniques in cardiac patients. The Cardiology Division of the Geneva University Hospital has assembled a minicomputer-based data acquisition/visualisation system to study cardiac structures and their associated motions using radionuclide techniques."},
